# Owner-evidence inventory (plan 05-01, D-26, D-28). One line per item that needs physical hardware (D10) or an owner system image (D11).
# Format: <id> | <discrepancy id> | <what the owner records> | <anchor in docs/input/d10-procedure.md, or docs/stic/d10-procedure.md for the D10-VID items and D11-EXEC-03>
# Rules (checked by the discrepancies step, tools/check/kinds/discrepancy.cmake): every open or partial discrepancy whose resolver starts
# `measurement:` is named by at least one line (token discrepancies-d10-missing); a line names an existing discrepancy, and a D10 line names one
# that is open or partial (token discrepancies-d10-unknown; D11 lines are checked for existence only). Keep a line free of semicolons and brackets.
# Nothing here has been measured or run: these are items handed to the owner, and no claim uses the measured-hardware tier.
D10-SYS-01 | C1 | STIC register access window after the vertical-blank interrupt, edges by cycle count | #system-probes
